WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
Far above the atmosphere, satellites
measure the sunlight arriving from the Sun.

2
00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:10.990
On a surface facing the rays head-on, that
intensity is called the solar constant.

3
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.890
Yet climate models start from
a figure only a quarter as big.

4
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.560
The Sun hasn't changed.

5
00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.030
So why the factor of four?

6
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.420
In this mission, you'll balance the power
a planet absorbs against the power it

7
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:23.990
emits.

8
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.730
Then you'll find how much sunlight
Earth scatters straight back into space,

9
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.700
and why that changes with cloud and ice.

10
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.400
Your mission: work out where
the factor of four comes from.
